# Trivy vulnerability exemptions for the service production images.
#
# This mirrors the npm-audit gate's exemption list in scripts/audit-bulk.mjs.
# Both scanners must agree: an advisory that is un-actionable there (no reachable
# patched version) is equally un-actionable in the image scan. Keep the two lists
# in sync — remove an entry here the moment its audit-bulk counterpart is removed.
#
# CVE-2026-14257 / GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg — brace-expansion OOM DoS.
#   Patched only in brace-expansion 5.0.8; the 2.x line ends at 2.1.2 with no
#   further release. 2.x consumers (minimatch@5/9) cannot be force-bumped to 5.x
#   without an API-compatibility audit, so pnpm.overrides pins the 2.x range to
#   2.1.2 (its safest reachable version) rather than crossing three majors.
#   Un-actionable per the workflow's stated policy ("only gate on CVEs that have
#   an upstream patch"). Unblock when upstream ships 2.1.3, or when the 2.x
#   consumers can safely move to brace-expansion 5.x.
CVE-2026-14257
